>> title: Onion Gravy
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: onion, gravy, southern, pan sauce, stovetop
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: brown onion gravy, smothering gravy, smothered gravy, brown gravy
>> servings: 6
>> time: 50 min
>> pairs-with: smothered-pork-chops, baked-turkey-wings, meatloaf
>> step.1: Brown the onions all the way to the colour you want the gravy to be. This is the whole of the flavour and there is nothing later in the recipe that can put it back.
>> step.2: brown the onions 25 min
>> step.3: stir the flour in 3 min
>> step.4: whisk in stock, simmer 12 min

Brown the onions all the way to the colour you want the gravy to be. This is the whole of the flavour and there is nothing later in the recipe that can put it back.

Melt @bacon fat{3%Tbs}(40 g) with @yellow onions{3%large}(1 1/2 lb / 700 g; sliced thin) in a #heavy skillet{} and cook them down for ~brown{25%min}.

Stir @&(~1)browned onions{} with @all-purpose flour{3%Tbs}(24 g) for ~stir{3%min}, until the flour smells toasted rather than raw.

Whisk @&(~1)onion roux{} with @beef stock{3%cup}(710 mL), @Worcestershire sauce{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%tsp} and ~simmer{12%min}.

Season it after it has reduced rather than before. Three cups goes down to two, and salt added at the start arrives at the table twice as strong as you meant it.
